
# 5 Analysis Models

This section expands on what has to exist inside our system for the use cases in section 4 to happen, and how those parts talk to each other.

## 5.1 Domain Model
| Class | What it represents (one line) | Key attributes | Associations (with multiplicity |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Student | Primary Actor | studentID, name, studentEmail | Student 0..*--1 LMS, Student 1 -- 0..* Enrollment, Student 1 -- 0..* Submission |
| LMS | Supporting Actor | name, unavailableMessage | LMS 1--0..* Student, LMS--Enrollment, LMS--Course |
| Course | Primary material for selected course | courseID | Course--LMS, Course 1--0..* Enrollment, Course 1--0..* Announcements, Course 1--0..*Assignment, Course 1--0..* Enrollment |
| Enrollment | Enrollment status | enrollmentDate, status | Enrollment -- LMS, Enrollment 0..*--1 Student, Enrollment 0..*--1 Course |
| Assignment | Primary material for selected assignment | asgnTitle, asgnDescription, dueDate | Assignment 0..*--1 Course, Assignment 1--0..* Submission |
| Submission | Material for student submission to selected assignment | sTitle, fileType, fileLink, timeSubmitted | Submission 0..*--1 Student, Submission 0..*--1 Assignment |
| Grade | Feedback on submission, from professor | feedback | Grade 0..1--1 Submission |
| Announcement | Announcements of upcoming assignments, quizzes, etc. | annTitle, annDescription | Announcement 0..*--1 Course |
